From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:18:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Set PLL_AUDIO0 to its 22.5792
 MHz x 4 point

The first 44.1 kHz stream on an I2S/PCM controller after boot fails:

  sun4i-i2s 2532000.i2s: Unsupported BCLK divider: -22

The I2S/PCM module clocks select AUDIO0PLL4X after reset, and sun4i-i2s
enables its module clock in runtime resume, before hw_params sets the
rate. PLL_AUDIO0 is CLK_SET_RATE_GATE, so while it is prepared its rate
is fixed at the reset value, about 98.3 MHz. The request for
22.5792 MHz then settles on PERI0_200M / 9, 22.22 MHz, for which no
BCLK divider exists. The failed attempt leaves the module clock on
PERI0_200M, PLL_AUDIO0 is released, and every later stream gets the
exact rate.

Set PLL_AUDIO0 to 90.3168 MHz when the CCU registers, the one point of
its sigma-delta table and the 22.5792 MHz x 4 configuration of the
manual's PLL table. No consumer holds the PLL at that time, so the rate
changes with the output gated, as the manual's frequency change
procedure requires. The 48 kHz family runs from PLL_AUDIO1 and is not
affected.

Not covered: CLK_SET_RATE_GATE stays; it matches the manual's procedure.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: after a cold boot PLL_AUDIO0 holds the
manual's point before any stream, and the first 44.1 kHz stream on
I2S/PCM0-4 and on OWA runs from AUDIO0PLL4X.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 3e52b38f1c4f..892c50f16680 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -583,6 +583,8 @@ ccu: clock-controller@2002000 {
 				      "iosc", "losc-fanout";
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
+			assigned-clocks = <&ccu CLK_PLL_AUDIO0_4X>;
+			assigned-clock-rates = <90316800>;
 		};
 
 		wdt: watchdog@2050000 {
